{%- comment -%}
  AJ PDP Spotlight — tells a product page when it is the one that matters today.

  THE PROBLEM. The homepage frames the Yoink of the Day and the Tee of the Week
  properly: an eyebrow, a clock, a saving, a reason to act now. The PRODUCT page
  for those same items was a stock Horizon PDP, identical to the other 2,700.
  So the moment an ad or a search result dropped someone straight onto it —
  which is exactly where paid traffic lands — every bit of that framing was
  gone. The card ad promises a sealed collector's tee and the page delivers a
  t-shirt at $25.50.

  WHAT THIS IS NOT. It does not rebuild the PDP or add a second buy box. The
  price, the variant picker and the add-to-cart below it are already good and
  duplicating them would make the page longer and the decision harder. This is a
  band above them that answers one question: why is this one different, and how
  long have I got.

  RESOLVES THE SAME WAY THE HOMEPAGE DOES, deliberately. The deal comes from
  walking `daily_deal` metaobject entries for the window containing now, exactly
  as `aj-daily-deal.liquid` does — not from a tag someone has to remember to
  set. If the two ever disagreed, the page and the homepage would tell a visitor
  different things about the same product.

  THE COUNTDOWN IS THE SHARED SNIPPET, not a copy. `aj-deal-countdown` renders
  an absolute server-side deadline, so the clock is the same for everyone and a
  refresh does not restart it. A per-session timer is the deceptive-urgency
  pattern this store has deliberately not built — and on an account that has
  already been suspended once for misrepresentation, inventing one here would be
  a spectacular own goal.

  RENDERS NOTHING on every other product. No wrapper, no padding, no empty band.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign now = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign deal = null
  for entry in shop.metaobjects.daily_deal.values
    assign starts = entry.starts_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign ends = entry.ends_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    if starts <= now and ends > now
      assign deal = entry
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign mode = ''
  if deal != null and deal.product.value.id == product.id
    assign mode = 'yoink'
  endif

  comment
    The tee is whatever sits first in the collection the agent maintains, which
    is the same source the homepage section reads. Checked second so a product
    that somehow managed to be both gets the stronger framing.
  endcomment
  if mode == blank
    assign tee_collection = collections['tee-of-the-week']
    if tee_collection != blank and tee_collection.products.first.id == product.id
      assign mode = 'tee'
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if mode != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    assign was = v.compare_at_price
    assign save_pct = 0
    if was > v.price
      assign save_pct = was | minus: v.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: was | round
    endif
  -%}

  <aside class="aj-spot aj-spot--{{ mode }}">
    <div class="page-width">
      <div class="aj-spot__inner">
        <div class="aj-spot__say">
          {%- if mode == 'yoink' -%}
            <p class="aj-spot__eyebrow">Today&rsquo;s Yoink</p>
            <p class="aj-spot__line">
              One thing goes on sale every day at a deep discount. Today it is this one.
              {%- if was > v.price %}
                When the clock runs out the price goes back to
                <strong>{{ was | money }}</strong>.
              {%- endif -%}
            </p>
          {%- else -%}
            <p class="aj-spot__eyebrow">Tee of the Week</p>
            <p class="aj-spot__line">
              One graphic tee gets sealed up every week. This is the one.
              When it rotates it goes back in the binder and another takes its place.
              <a class="aj-spot__link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}collections/tee-past">See the whole set &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if save_pct > 0 -%}
          <p class="aj-spot__save">
            <span class="aj-spot__save-num">{{ save_pct }}%</span>
            <span class="aj-spot__save-word">off</span>
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          NO CLOCK HERE. The product-information block already renders a
          "Deal ends in" countdown in the buy box, a few centimetres below. Two
          identical timers on one screen reads as a bug, and the one beside the
          add-to-cart is the one doing the work. This band supplies the framing
          the buy box cannot: what kind of thing this is, and what the price
          returns to.
        {%- endcomment -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </aside>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    A band, not a hero. It sits between the header and the product and has to
    read as a label ON this page rather than as a competing page of its own —
    the add-to-cart is the thing that matters and it is directly below.
  */
  .aj-spot {
    padding-block: 1.1rem;
    margin-block-end: 0.5rem;
  }

  /*
    THE BAND IS FULL-BLEED, ITS CONTENTS ARE NOT. `.page-width` centres a column
    but does not inset it here, so the eyebrow sat hard against the viewport
    edge while the header and the product below it aligned to the grid — the one
    element on the page that looked unplaced. `--page-margin` is the theme's own
    gutter (16px on a phone, 40px from 750px up), so this tracks it rather than
    guessing a number that drifts.
  */
  .aj-spot .page-width {
    padding-inline: var(--page-margin, 16px);
  }

  .aj-spot--yoink {
    background: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    color: #fff;
  }

  /* Cyan hairlines top and bottom, the same edge treatment as the collector
     slab on the homepage card. It is the one visual cue that ties this page to
     the ad someone just clicked. */
  .aj-spot--tee {
    background: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    color: #fff;
    border-block: 3px solid var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8);
  }

  .aj-spot__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 2rem;
  }

  .aj-spot__say {
    flex: 1 1 22rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /*
    Ohpixel, uppercase, yellow — the same eyebrow the homepage deal block uses.
    The face has no lowercase and no star glyph, which is why this is set in
    caps rather than title case.
  */
  .aj-spot__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  .aj-spot--tee .aj-spot__eyebrow {
    color: var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8);
  }

  .aj-spot__line {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .aj-spot__line strong {
    /* The restored price is the honest part of the urgency, so it is the one
       thing in the sentence allowed to shout. */
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .aj-spot__link {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-block-end: 1px solid currentcolor;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .aj-spot__save {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .aj-spot__save-num {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  .aj-spot--tee .aj-spot__save-num {
    color: #fff;
  }

  .aj-spot__save-word {
    font-size: 1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  /*
    ON A PHONE the band must not push the price and the add-to-cart below the
    fold — that is the whole reason paid traffic is landing here. Tighter
    padding, and the saving sits beside the clock rather than starting a row of
    its own.
  */
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .aj-spot {
      padding-block: 0.85rem;
    }

    .aj-spot__inner {
      gap: 0.6rem 1rem;
    }

    .aj-spot__line {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Deal spotlight (PDP)",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Appears only on the product that is currently the Yoink of the Day or the Tee of the Week. Every other product page renders nothing. The deal is resolved from the daily_deal metaobject, the same source the homepage uses, so the two can never disagree."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Deal spotlight (PDP)" }]
}
{% endschema %}
